permitfrom = Dr. J.A. Farrer, Ingleborough Estate Office, Clapham, via Lancaster.
description = This is LUSS's adopted cave which means every so often we run a trip to try and
description = pick up some of the litter which accumulates. It can be found
description = approximately 650 metres North North West of Trow Gill. The first pitch
description = is constricted at the top, but soon opens out to a cavern with the
description = floor 17 metres below. From here the main route onwards is a hole in
description = the floor, and down over a large smooth slab. It is often usefull to
description = have a rope for this. Continuing onward and to the left the passage
description = slopes downward and leads under a rock bridge. Clambering through a
description = hole in the floor leads to the head of the next pitch, with two main
description = belay points. The first is reached by decending a further 2 metres and
description = is often used for laddered descents, (it has a ledge about 1/3 of the
description = wy from the top) the other can be reached by continuing horizonatally
description = for 4-5 metres to a traverse. This second provides an unbroken descent
description = (37m) and is good for SRT.

